  "biobricks:reviewed": false,
  "biobricks:reviewNotes": "Determined by BioBricks licensing-provenance annotation agent (Claude Opus 4.8). The download stage and README show the data comes from the NIH RePORTER ExPORTER bulk-export service (reporter.nih.gov/exporter), an official U.S. National Institutes of Health resource. NIH RePORTER/ExPORTER records are U.S. Government Works in the public domain and are published for open bulk download without registration, license fee, or restriction, so licenseClass=open and merckCommercialUse=permitted. The RePORTER FAQ/data-policy pages rendered only as JavaScript to the fetcher, so the public-domain determination is grounded in the U.S.-federal-agency provenance (a US Government Work) rather than a quoted RePORTER license badge; confidence is set accordingly. A reviewer may confirm the RePORTER data-availability statement and note NIH's request that any personally identifying investigator information be used responsibly.",
